  "jobTitle": "Software Engineer",
  "summary": "I graduated from UCSD with a degree in Electrical Engineering where I focused on semiconductor devices and materials while also building a foundation in programming, circuit simulation, instrumentation, and modeling tools. That mix of hardware and software fluency helped me land first role as a project engineer at Cyth Systems, where I've spent the past three years growing into a cross-disciplinary, systems-driven engineer. \n\n\n\nI'm a designer-engineer at heart. My work centers on understanding complex systems, shaping structure out of ambiguity, and delivering tools that work reliably in real environments. I've contributed across embedded software, automation, electrical integration,  and system architecture allowing me to lead projects that require everything from firmware design and protocol to sensor integration, and hardware-in-the-loop testing. That breadth has become one of my strengths as it lets me see how decisions in one domain ripple across an entire system. \n\n\n\nAlong the way, I've learned the human side of engineering  as I've been tasked with leading the coordination across EE, ME, and software teams, translating technical constraints into clear decisions, and keeping projects aligned when requirements shift or information is incomplete. These experiences have shaped me into someone who can lead with both technical depth and calm, structured communication. \n\n\n\nI'm now looking for opportunities where I can take on greater ownership in system architecture, integrate hardware and software, and build solutions that are elegant, durable, and thoughtfully engineered.",
